    <string name="about_title">About us</string>
    <string name="about_commitment">Our commitment to your crop</string>
    <string name="about_mission_t">Our mission</string>
    <string name="about_mission">Use artificial intelligence to empower growers in the early detection and control of damage such as scab, improving the quality and productivity of their gulupa crops.</string>
    <string name="about_team_t">Our team</string>
    <string name="about_course">Mobile Application Development · Universidad Nacional de Colombia</string>
    <string name="about_how_t">How it works</string>
    <string name="how1">Take or pick a clear, centered photo of the fruit.</string>
    <string name="how2">The AI detects the fruit and segments the damaged areas.</string>
    <string name="how3">Each damage type is classified automatically.</string>
    <string name="how4">Severity is quantified from the % of affected area.</string>
    <string name="how5">You get a summary with management recommendations.</string>
    <string name="about_scope_t">Model scope</string>
    <string name="about_scope">Current version: analysis uses the PowderyVision7 pipeline (YOLO11 + Chan-Vese segmentation), trained on pea and tomato leaves for powdery mildew. Gulupa damage (scab, mechanical damage, thrips) will appear once the model is trained on the fruit dataset; the app is already prepared to receive them.</string>
    <string name="about_base">Based on PowderyVision7 · J. E. Flores-Riera · Universidad Nacional de Colombia</string>
